From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 15:10:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ports/arkweb: IME / soft-keyboard integration

Connect the OHOS system input method to Servo, driven by Servo's
show/hide_embedder_control(EmbedderControl::InputMethod). ACE does not
push system-keyboard text into NWeb (WebPattern is not a TextInputClient;
OnInterceptKeyboardAttach defaults to useSystemKeyboard), so the engine
owns the IME connection itself. Servo does this via the public OHOS
InputMethod NDK through the ohos-ime crate, mirroring servoshell's OHOS
port: a ServoIme text-editor proxy forwards the IME insert/delete/enter
callbacks to the servo thread as Actions, delivered as InputEvent::Ime /
key events. Also override ServoNWeb::NeedSoftKeyboard (new
need_soft_keyboard bridge reading a per-webview ime_active flag) so ACE
performs keyboard-avoidance layout while an editable is focused.

Add ports/arkweb/tools/test_ime.py, an on-device smoke test (pytest +
hdc-py) that launches a self-describing data: page and drives the soft
keyboard. Servo renders web content to a GPU surface invisible to
UiTest, so it observes state via hilog markers and screenshot pixel
checks -- the page recolours its background to encode the field value,
making the value assertion OCR-free.

Validated on the rk3568 by running `uv run ports/arkweb/tools/test_ime.py`:
tap input -> keyboard shows + ACE avoidance; typed text enters the field;
backspace edits it; blur hides the keyboard and restores the web height;
no crash.

Validation: Test by running uv run ports/arkweb/tools/test_ime.py on a device (needs a default input method).
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implementation and on-device testing)
